    { math: '2 · Gauss (magnetic): no magnetic charge', note: 'Field lines through any closed box net to zero — magnetic field lines always close on themselves. There are no isolated north poles.' },
    { math: '3 · Faraday: changing B makes E', note: 'A time-varying magnetic field curls an electric field around itself — the generator equation.' },
    { math: '4 · Ampère–Maxwell: currents and changing E make B', note: 'Maxwell\'s addition (a changing electric field also curls a magnetic field) closed the loop: each field can regenerate the other.' },
    { math: '5 · The wave falls out', note: 'Self-regenerating E and B waves travel at 1/√(μ₀ε₀) = 3 × 10⁸ m/s — the measured speed of light. "Light is an electromagnetic disturbance." Maxwell, 1865.' },
